---
permalink: /overlay/live/
title: Live
bodyClass: overlay--live
---
{% from "components/panel.njk" import panel %}

{# The live scene. No backdrop - everything except these elements stays fully
   transparent so gameplay and the camera show through from the OBS sources
   underneath.

   Positions are in 1920x1080 space. Adjust here rather than moving the
   Browser Source in OBS, so the overlay and the camera stay in register. #}

{# Camera frame. Border only, transparent centre - your camera source sits
   BELOW this overlay in the OBS source list and shows through the hole.
   Default: 480x270 box in the bottom-right, 16:9. #}
<div class="ov-cam" style="right: 48px; bottom: 48px; width: 480px; height: 270px;">
  <span class="ov-cam__label" data-param="camlabel">Mitch</span>
</div>

{# Lower third. #}
<div class="ov-lower">
  {% call panel({
    variant: "dialog",
    banner: "Now",
    tone: "notice",
    title: "Building something",
    subtitle: "mtch.tech"
  }) %}
    <p style="margin:0;font-size:18px;color:var(--ov-muted)" data-param="lead">
      Working on the site. Ask anything.
    </p>
  {% endcall %}
</div>

{# Corner strip: clock plus a handle. #}
<div class="ov-strip">
  <span class="ov-strip__clock" data-clock>--:--</span>
  <span class="ov-strip__sep" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="ov-strip__handle" data-param="handle">@MitchDizzle</span>
</div>

{# Alert rail. Reuses the site's toast panel so future integrations look
   native rather than bolted on. Fire one while testing with:
     MitchOverlay.toast("Follower", "someone followed", "success") #}
<div class="panel-toasts" id="panel-toasts"></div>
